{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}$ is the *second derivative* of $y$. In other words, it's the derivative of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$, which is the derivative of $y$.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}$, we need to differentiate $y$ twice.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's start by finding $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{6}{x^2}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\dfrac{12}{x^3}\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{6}{x^2}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[6x^{-2}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=6\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[x^{-2}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=6\\left(-2x^{-3}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-12x^{-3}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\dfrac{12}{x^3}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"Now we can differentiate $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ to find $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-\\dfrac{12}{x^3}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{36}{x^4}\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-\\dfrac{12}{x^3}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-12x^{-3}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-12\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[x^{-3}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-12\\left(-3x^{-4}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=36x^{-4}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{36}{x^4}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}=\\dfrac{36}{x^4}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $y=\\dfrac{6}{x^2}$.\n\n**Find $\\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{36}{x^4}$","correct":true},{"content":"$\\dfrac{1}{x^4}$","correct":false},{"content":"$-\\dfrac{12}{x^3}$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$6\\ln(x)$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
